From e2cf5ac9c576413de4e3dbfedec66a7a7f266e7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:57:13 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: airoha: allocate LED state for the EN7512 GPHY

The EN7512 (and EN7521/EN7526) GPHY driver uses the mt798x LED callbacks,
which keep their state in phydev->priv, but its probe never allocated it.
With PHY LEDs described in DT the first brightness update oopses:

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address 00000000
  test_and_clear_bit+0x.. <- mtk_phy_hw_led_blink_set
  <- mt798x_phy_led_brightness_set <- set_brightness_delayed

Seen on the TP-Link XZ000-G3 v2 right after GPHY calibration.

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/mediatek/airoha-ge-soc.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/airoha-ge-soc.c b/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/airoha-ge-soc.c
index a0ba11fc3..fd40ef58e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/airoha-ge-soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/airoha-ge-soc.c
@@ -2523,6 +2523,14 @@ static int en7512_phy_calib(struct phy_device *phydev)
 
 static int en7512_phy_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
+	struct mtk_socphy_priv *priv;
+
+	/* The mt798x LED callbacks keep their state in phydev->priv. */
+	priv = devm_kzalloc(&phydev->mdio.dev, sizeof(*priv), GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!priv)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	phydev->priv = priv;
+
 	/* EN7512 has one standalone GPHY at MDIO address 12. */
 	return en7512_phy_calib(phydev);
 }
